{"duration_api_ms":73613,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"dc0a90c4-f816-48bc-be26-6e57ba146266","total_cost_usd":0.9649832,"usage":{"input_tokens":28,"cache_creation_input_tokens":77691,"cache_read_input_tokens":1035316,"output_tokens":6814,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1161},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":77691,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1087,"cache_read_input_tokens":89096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":387,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":387},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":28,"outputTokens":6814,"cacheReadInputTokens":1035316,"cacheCreationInputTokens":77691,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9649832,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1161,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":15,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I requested changes on CR rev1 of TASK-260922-vcx6yo. The verdict is recorded with `reject_cr`, the task is back in `to-dev`, and the verdict is attached as `TASK-260922-vcx6yo_review-verdict-rev1.md`. The task only admits a second client under the required capabilities in the specific cases the tests happen to cover.\n\n**What I ran:** the `termbind` and `tmuxserver` package tests on the candidate tree (`2a23b9f`) both pass. I then planted 6 weakened versions (\"narrowings\") of the gates in `ops.go`, plus one harmless control, and 4 of the 6 were caught by a named test:\n\n| Narrowing | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Admission lock removed entirely | caught |\n| Lock released before the receipt is written | caught |\n| `multi_attach` skipped when both clients are read-only | caught |\n| Same-client replay exemption turned off | caught |\n| Lock taken only for input-authorized attaches | **not caught** |\n| `multiple_input_clients` checked only against the first peer | **not caught** |\n\n**Findings:**\n- **P1 – concurrent read-only attaches:** The only concurrency test uses a writable first client. With the lock skipped for read-only attaches, two concurrent read-only clients on an instance without `multi_attach` could both be admitted. Both would get a receipt and a vector. That is the read-only-no-multi scenario from the 1c28dz rev7 review, reached through a race.\n- **P2 – input check only against the first peer:** Every `multiple_input_clients` test has exactly one input-authorized peer, and it is always first in client-ID order. Suppose a read-only peer sorts first, an input-authorized peer sorts second, and a new input-authorized client arrives. If the check looked only at the first peer, that new client would be admitted and no test would fail.\n- **P3 – census overstates coverage:** The gate × entry census rates the lock gate as tested, but its only test row is a writable one. It needs re-deriving once the new tests exist.\n\n**No findings:**\n- A client whose liveness can't be proven is still treated as a possible peer.\n- The new `.admission.lock` file is skipped by the existing peer census instead of creating a second census.\n- The Windows lock implementation reads correctly.\n\n**Not verified by me:** the full repo suite, the Windows `go vet` run, the run with tmux unavailable, and the outcome comparison across importing packages. For those I only have the producer's attached validation log.\n\n**Rework scope for the producer:**\n1. Add a paused concurrent test with two read-only clients and no `multi_attach`. It must produce exactly one receipt and one vector, and fail if the lock is taken only for input-authorized attaches.\n2. Add a concurrent-input test where the input-authorized peer is not first in client-ID order. It must refuse and write no receipt.\n3. Update the census and the requirements coverage table (the conformance matrix) with the tests that catch these two narrowings.\n\nI set the status to `to-dev` by hand before finding `reject_cr`, which also routes to `to-dev`. So the board history shows a status change before the CR verdict, but the end state is the same.","ttft_ms":2889,"type":"result","duration_ms":236248,"uuid":"08076721-5abe-43ce-8cf0-1a424e41a093","ttft_stream_ms":1653,"time_to_request_ms":25,"first_content_frame_ms":1653,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
